      "lines": [
        {
          "x": 269,
          "y": 208,
          "width": 120,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "PART B1",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 257,
          "width": 963,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "Read Text 3 and answer questions 32-41 on pages 1-2 of the Question-Answer Book for Part B1.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 302,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "Text 3",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 641,
          "y": 359,
          "width": 269,
          "height": 22,
          "text": "Witness Statement",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 268,
          "y": 423,
          "width": 648,
          "height": 22,
          "text": "I, Anna Rossi, of 3 Arthur Street, Yau Ma Tei, housewife, state:",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 472,
          "width": 1016,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "On 1 December 2014 at about 3:30pm, I was about to get into my car in the car park next to the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 502,
          "width": 339,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "shops on Wood Road, Wan Chai.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 363,
          "y": 546,
          "width": 577,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "that a silver car was driving down the aisle behind me.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 590,
          "width": 1017,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "I saw a green sports car reverse out of a car space and collide with the silver car. The silver car",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 620,
          "width": 411,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "was moving at the time of the collision.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 664,
          "width": 620,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "My car was parked opposite where the accident happened.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 267,
          "y": 709,
          "width": 1015,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "Both the drivers got out of their cars. Neither of them seemed to be hurt and I went over to",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 738,
          "width": 289,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "them to see how they were.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 782,
          "width": 1016,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "The driver of the green car said “Did you see the accident?” | said words to the effect “I saw it”.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 812,
          "width": 1016,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "He then said “Can you give me your contact details, just in case | need a statement from you?” I",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 841,
          "width": 514,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "replied “Yes”. | then gave him my contact details.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 886,
          "width": 198,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "It was a sunny day.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 930,
          "width": 1017,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "The speed limit in the car park was 20km per hour. The silver car was travelling at about 40km",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 959,
          "width": 95,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "per hour.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 266,
          "y": 1003,
          "width": 641,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "I noticed damage to the back left side of the green sports car.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 1048,
          "width": 681,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "I believe that the contents of this statement are true and correct.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 1092,
          "width": 167,
          "height": 22,
          "text": "Signed: A. Rossi",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 1120,
          "width": 262,
          "height": 19,
          "text": "Dated: 7 December 2014",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1230,
          "width": 959,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "Read Text 4 and answer questions 42-55 on pages 2-4 of the Question-Answer Book for Part BI",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1289,
          "width": 61,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "Text 4",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 525,
          "y": 1332,
          "width": 495,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "Will cars with no drivers catch on?",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 1411,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "[1] Some day in the near future, cars will drive themselves. Traffic jams and deadly accidents will",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1444,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "become a thing of the past. Driving to work will be less stressful, as riders can sit back with their",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1477,
          "width": 400,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "coffee and let computers handle the trip.",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 265,
          "y": 1531,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "[2] That’s the dream of many, at least. And it’s not totally unrealistic. Google is developing",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 263,
          "y": 1560,
          "width": 1001,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "“autonomous vehicles” that are improving rapidly each year. A future of completely self-driving",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 263,
          "y": 1590,
          "width": 331,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "vehicles doesn’t seem too far off.",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1639,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "[3] And yet, according to a new report by the Eno Center for Transportation, there are still many",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 263,
          "y": 1668,
          "width": 705,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "obstacles to overcome before self-driving cars take over our highways.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 264,
          "y": 1717,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "[4] “Self-driving cars have the potential to transform transport as we know it,” explained report",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 263,
          "y": 1745,
          "width": 1001,
          "height": 25,
          "text": "co-author Daniel Fagnant — and bring billions of dollars’ worth of benefits. But getting to that point",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 213,
          "y": 1748,
          "width": 20,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "10",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1776,
          "width": 142,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "won't be easy.",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 218,
          "y": 1999,
          "width": 568,
          "height": 19,
          "text": "2015-DSE-ENG LANG 1I-B1-RP-2 2",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "width": 1489,
      "height": 2106,
      "label": "Reading passage page 2",
      "lines": [
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 200,
          "width": 335,
          "height": 22,
          "text": "The benefits of self-driving cars",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 242,
          "width": 997,
          "height": 34,
          "text": "[5] It’s easy to list the benefits of a world with self-driving vehicles. Safety is the biggest. Right now,",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 275,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "more than 30,000 people die each year in the United States from automobile crashes. And roughly 40",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 303,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "percent of fatal accidents are caused by alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue. Letting robots take the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 211,
          "y": 308,
          "width": 19,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "15",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 335,
          "width": 235,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "wheel would save lives.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 382,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "[6] Or take congestion. Cars driven by robots could travel closer together at steadier speeds. They",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 411,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 25,
          "text": "wouldn’t bunch up in traffic jams caused by aripple of brake lights. More cars could squeeze onto the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 260,
          "y": 437,
          "width": 716,
          "height": 32,
          "text": "road and move more quickly, and a lot of time and fuel would be saved.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 489,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[7] If just 10 percent of the vehicles on the road were self-driving cars, the authors estimate, the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 494,
          "width": 23,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "20",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 513,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 34,
          "text": "country could save more than $37 billion a year — fewer deaths, less fuel, more free time. If we",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 546,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "reached a point where 90 percent of the cars on the road were self-driving vehicles, the benefits would",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 578,
          "width": 335,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "rise to around $450 billion a year.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 625,
          "width": 997,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[8] Now, as Fagnant pointed out in a presentation, these are “ballpark, rough estimates...guesses,",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 654,
          "width": 953,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "really.” So don’t get too fixated on the numbers. They’re meant to be illustrative, not definitive.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 659,
          "width": 22,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "25",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 704,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "[9] The authors also didn’t try to quantify any of the costs of self-driving vehicles. What’s the price",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 260,
          "y": 733,
          "width": 613,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "tag on these gadgets? How does that compare to the benefits?",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 782,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[10] And what about unforeseen consequences? Researchers can’t predict how, exactly, self-driving",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 811,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "cars might reshape society. Maybe the vehicles will induce even more travel and congestion will get",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 840,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "worse. Or maybe they will lead to an increase in air pollution. It’s impossible to know at this point.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 844,
          "width": 23,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "30",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 871,
          "width": 353,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "Still, the advantages are tantalizing.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 922,
          "width": 352,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "The problems of self-driving cars",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 968,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "[11] Even if the benefits are many, self-driving vehicles have a lot of hoops to leap through. First, the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 260,
          "y": 997,
          "width": 1002,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "technology is still very pricey. By one estimate, the first wave of autonomous vehicles could cost over",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1026,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 25,
          "text": "$100,000 — five times the cost of the average new vehicle. Even that might be an underestimate: the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 1030,
          "width": 22,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "35",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1055,
          "width": 672,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "3-D sensors alone on Google’s autonomous car cost about $70,000.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1103,
          "width": 998,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[12] Those costs would presumably come down over time, but no one knows how rapidly. And that’s",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1131,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "a big hurdle. One survey found that only 20 percent of Americans would “definitely” or “probably”",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1161,
          "width": 758,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "buy a car with self-driving capabilities even if the price dropped to $30,000.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1210,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[13] What’s more, while the technology is rapidly improving, it’s far from perfect. Google’s",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 1215,
          "width": 23,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "40",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1238,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "self-driving cars have now traveled more than 435,000 miles in California, but the cars have yet to be",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1271,
          "width": 345,
          "height": 23,
          "text": "fully tested in urban environments.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1315,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 47,
          "text": "[14] Most likely, self-driving technology will emerge gradually, piece by pices: But even",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1348,
          "width": 451,
          "height": 25,
          "text": "intermediate features pose unique challenges.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1397,
          "width": 999,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "[15] Early autonomous cars will likely require their human drivers to take the wheel during especially",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 208,
          "y": 1401,
          "width": 22,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "45",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1426,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "complicated situations. But as one car maker is discovering, it’s difficult to get people to drift in and",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1454,
          "width": 1001,
          "height": 26,
          "text": "out of attention while driving —and the process of switching back and forth between robot and",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1485,
          "width": 515,
          "height": 22,
          "text": "human could well make these cars less safe, at first.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1533,
          "width": 1003,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "[16] The Eno report also notes that there’s still a ton of research yet to be done about the prospect of",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1562,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 27,
          "text": "self-driving cars. “As long as crucial questions go unanswered,” the report concludes, “the nation will",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 209,
          "y": 1567,
          "width": 22,
          "height": 18,
          "text": "50",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1590,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 28,
          "text": "be hampered in its ability to successfully plan for and introduce [autonomous vehicles] into the",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 261,
          "y": 1623,
          "width": 229,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "transportation system.”",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 582,
          "y": 1748,
          "width": 359,
          "height": 21,
          "text": "END OF READING PASSAGES",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1809,
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 25,
          "text": "Sources of materials used in this paper will be acknowledged in the Examination Report and Question Papers",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 262,
          "y": 1837,
          "width": 769,
          "height": 24,
          "text": "published by the Hong Kong Examinations and Assessment Authority at a later stage.",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 779,
          "y": 2002,
          "width": 10,
          "height": 17,
          "text": "w",
          "bold": false
        },
        {
          "x": 218,
